  "findings": [],
  "checked_arguments": [
    {
      "item": "actual weak equations",
      "result": "mixed_grushin_y_equations assumes only the zero-word weak (P_c+B) equation. Finite spectator differentiation and local potential reduction yield P_c F[[],b]=S[[],b] minus the full spectator product. Two actual same-direction spectator integrations then yield P_0 F[[],b]=S[[],b] minus the product plus c|y|^2 sum_j F[[],j::j::b]. Finite Y differentiation uses actual bundled local weak chains for both sides; no positive-order PDE is a hypothesis of the final potential-step wrapper."
    },
    {
      "item": "sign and basis bridge",
      "result": "The source is S minus mixedPotentialWordProduct plus c times the directional word product of |y|^2 and the spectator diagonal sum. This agrees with P_c=-Delta_Y-c|y|^2 Delta_T. The explicit basisFun-to-oscillatorBasis equality is proved pointwise before applying the local potential reduction."
    },
    {
      "item": "triangular derivative availability",
      "result": "Every solution entry used by a source at (a,b) has Y length at most |a|<=r and total length at most |a|+|b|+2<=m. Finite mixed spectator chains are derived from existing Y chains and pure spectator chains by actual weak commutation. No unavailable Y order greater than r or total order m+1 is imported."
    },
    {
      "item": "odd and even extension edges",
      "result": "Fnext retains every old Y length<=r exactly. Its new length r+1 entries use recovered ordered second jets at predecessor length r-1; new length r+2 entries use predecessor length r. The hgain filter restricts to these two predecessor levels and total order<=m-2. hAttach identifies a recovered first representative with the existing first derivative by local AE uniqueness. The final transition from new r+1 to r+2 similarly attaches compatible first representatives. Both odd and even boundaries are covered."
    },
    {
      "item": "norm budget and missing first-jet bound",
      "result": "Only recovered second jets become new Fnext entries, so no unproved uniform norm bound on the auxiliary recovered first jets is needed. A single component is bounded by the nonnegative ordered-second aggregate, which is <=(3/2)*(C0*W+C1*R). The max with W preserves old entries. C0=4*A^2+16*L*(D/2+Q) and C1=2*M^2+8*L*D are nonnegative from the supplied geometric L,D,Q hypotheses."
    },
    {
      "item": "source and coefficient quantitative orders",
      "result": "The final potential-step wrapper requests source region budgets and mixed coefficient pointwise budgets only for |a|+|b|+2<=m, and source chain steps only while that sum is strictly below m. The rectangular coefficient inputs to the fixed-word source estimate fit within that total range. The quadratic coefficient budget is requested only through |a|+2<=m."
    },
    {
      "item": "explicit source budget",
      "result": "The fixed source bound is 3*H+3*(2^(|a|+|b|))^2*K^2*W+3*c^2*(2^|a|)^2*card(kappa)^2*Q0^2*W. Replacing both word powers by 2^m uses W>=0 and yields exactly mixedYSourceBudget after ring normalization. Duplicate Leibniz splits are retained; the spectator trace contributes card(kappa)^2. No source H>=0 premise is needed for the exponent comparison because 3*H is unchanged."
    },
